# Sidecar ignore file for sdk/python/Dockerfile.
#
# A `<Dockerfile>.dockerignore` REPLACES the repository root `.dockerignore`
# entirely for this build — it does not merge with it. That is the point: the
# root file excludes `sdk`, so a build using the repository root as its context
# cannot see the package it exists to test, and the failure reads as a missing
# directory rather than as an ignore rule.
#
# So this file starts from "exclude everything" and admits exactly what the
# image needs. The package's own sources are NOT among them: they arrive on the
# gate's /repo mount, so a change to src/ or tests/ never invalidates a layer.
*

# The pre-compiled engine library, built by `make capi-lib`. Gitignored, and
# the root ignore file never mentioned it because nothing else needs it.
!dist/capi/local
